(880561, 97763, 11832, '<td valign="top">very very cool.</td>', 'very very cool.', '2004-08-27 17:59:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(880581, 97763, 1031, '<td valign="top">Cool picture -- to be logically consistent with your title, you might consider reversing the desaturation (have the part in the lens B+W), since the "rest of us" would just see pretty flowers, while the botanist might see the structure/anatomy in a more coolly clinical manner.</td>', 'Cool picture -- to be logically consistent with your title, you might consider reversing the desaturation (have the part in the lens B+W), since the "rest of us" would just see pretty flowers, while the botanist might see the structure/anatomy in a more coolly clinical manner.', '2004-08-27 18:12:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(881092, 97605, 24494, '<td valign="top">156th!!!!<br/> <br/>i gave you a 9 great shot</td>', '156th!!!! i gave you a 9 great shot', '2004-08-28 01:06:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(882055, 98023, 10390, '<td valign="top">Well, this was a last "microsecond entry", the last hours I decided to to something for this challenge because a friend of mine loaned a macro lens to me, I got a good an idea working with leaves, worked with it for 2 hours and sadly it didn''t work out very good.  <br/>Here in Iceland the challenge entry time is out at 4am.  At almost 3:30 I was very disapointed with what I got so far, then I just thought I had to submit something, I didn''t just been awake for no reason.  So where I sat at my computer I took one of the leaves, but a hole in a paper and put the leaf there so it would be standing, moved a lamp to make this shadow and took some shots.  Then I put the photos in the computer and was trying to decide which photo to submit.  All of a sudden I saw that I only had few minutes ''till the submission time expired. I had to work very quick and when I was finally clicking on the submit button the time on my computer said 4:01am, and right after I clicked the button a error message came up that said the page requested couldn''t be displayed because the submission time had expired. I was disappointed, decided to check out what others had submitted, and then I discovered that my photo was there in the challenge!  The time must have expired just a microsecond after I submitted the photo.<br/>I think the photo is technically ok, but it isn''t interesting enough and didn''t deserve a higher position.  I don''t complain about the 5.565/58% it got.</td>', 'Well, this was a last "microsecond entry", the last hours I decided to to something for this challenge because a friend of mine loaned a macro lens to me, I got a good an idea working with leaves, worked with it for 2 hours and sadly it didn''t work out very good.  Here in Iceland the challenge entry time is out at 4am.  At almost 3:30 I was very disapointed with what I got so far, then I just thought I had to submit something, I didn''t just been awake for no reason.  So where I sat at my computer I took one of the leaves, but a hole in a paper and put the leaf there so it would be standing, moved a lamp to make this shadow and took some shots.  Then I put the photos in the computer and was trying to decide which photo to submit.  All of a sudden I saw that I only had few minutes ''till the submission time expired. I had to work very quick and when I was finally clicking on the submit button the time on my computer said 4:01am, and right after I clicked the button a error message came up that said the page requested couldn''t be displayed because the submission time had expired. I was disappointed, decided to check out what others had submitted, and then I discovered that my photo was there in the challenge!  The time must have expired just a microsecond after I submitted the photo.I think the photo is technically ok, but it isn''t interesting enough and didn''t deserve a higher position.  I don''t complain about the 5.565/58% it got.', '2004-08-29 00:31:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(882056, 96797, 24846, '<td valign="top">VERY VERY nice dont get why you didnt get first.<br/> <br/>So did you end up cooking it? LoL</td>', 'VERY VERY nice dont get why you didnt get first. So did you end up cooking it? LoL', '2004-08-29 00:31:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(882168, 97980, 5585, '<td valign="top">For all the people who asked about why this picture.... I work in a place where we do alot of walking....earning our living.. servicing the slot machines in a busy Casino... some people need HIP replacements..... I have a problem I have to deal with in the next month.. I will be off work 6 weeks... it is NOT a Knee Replacement...I lift heavy bags of coin and rush around the Casino with a bright and happy face...dealing with angry losers and impatient winners...lol..so when I saw the Botany Challenge I was trying to be funny as always and sarcastic...tried to take the best picture possible.. an come across with an thought provoking image...displaying a Casino Employee''s plight with their lousy...insurance...and the  fact that we all break down... if we work beyond what our bodies allow us... Pretty sticky situation... hence  the Cactus plant... double edge sword...you know.. "Bought a Knee"....BOTANY... Thanx</td>', 'For all the people who asked about why this picture.... I work in a place where we do alot of walking....earning our living.. servicing the slot machines in a busy Casino... some people need HIP replacements..... I have a problem I have to deal with in the next month.. I will be off work 6 weeks... it is NOT a Knee Replacement...I lift heavy bags of coin and rush around the Casino with a bright and happy face...dealing with angry losers and impatient winners...lol..so when I saw the Botany Challenge I was trying to be funny as always and sarcastic...tried to take the best picture possible.. an come across with an thought provoking image...displaying a Casino Employee''s plight with their lousy...insurance...and the  fact that we all break down... if we work beyond what our bodies allow us... Pretty sticky situation... hence  the Cactus plant... double edge sword...you know.. "Bought a Knee"....BOTANY... Thanx', '2004-08-29 04:35:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(882742, 97704, 6999, '<td valign="top">From an occasional critique clubber ...<br/> <br/>Quite why so very many people decided that a Botany challenge should be a Flower challenge defeats me ... but you''ve nevertheless done an OK job with this. Your notes are useful in telling why it didn''t do better, actually - I can''t imagine that ''auto'' both levels and contrast is really going to give you satisfying texture in your final image - they are processes designed to bring everything to visibility, and real depth of texture and detail in a shot require a great deal more fine-tuning. I would imagine that playing with the other controls in PS would give you some idea of what you might have got out of the shot; certainly in a dpc-friendly sense - the shot needs more sense of drama - more progression of light and shade, more three-dimensionality, than it has.<br/> <br/>I also think your sense of composition here is slightly askew - in that this is a very straightforward depiction of the flower. A good look through all the winning shots shows that there is a much more intense focus on shadow work, on a sense of landscape in the shots that have scored well than you have achieved here. Imagine, if you had focussed more clearly on the centre of the flower, and used the outer petals to frame that area, you would have the recognisable subject all the same, but with more immediate photographic impact.<br/> <br/>All of which presumes you are aiming simply to score well here, rather than submitting for any other reason.<br/> <br/>Outside of dpc-world, there is a feeling of odd light that I like very much in the centre of the flower: the very centre of the stamens seems to glow, and gives the impression of the flower emerging from the light of that area. However, even in this sense, I think you still need a greater sense of light and shade in the image. Along the stems of the petals there doesn''t seem to be much graduation between what should have been light areas and should have been dark ones - again, I suspect that this is as much a function of the auto-thing as of your capture of the image. Also, the inclusion of the greenery works against this - making more of the fact that it is simply a flower, rather than of the extraordinary elements at it''s centre - and puts the shot into a different category - one that is more of simple illustration. Whilst there is nothing wrong with that, it never seems to do that well here. <br/> <br/>It could perhaps have been worked into something that would have scored better, but as it stands, i think if fully deserving of it''s ''average'' score.<br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'From an occasional critique clubber ... Quite why so very many people decided that a Botany challenge should be a Flower challenge defeats me ... but you''ve nevertheless done an OK job with this. Your notes are useful in telling why it didn''t do better, actually - I can''t imagine that ''auto'' both levels and contrast is really going to give you satisfying texture in your final image - they are processes designed to bring everything to visibility, and real depth of texture and detail in a shot require a great deal more fine-tuning. I would imagine that playing with the other controls in PS would give you some idea of what you might have got out of the shot; certainly in a dpc-friendly sense - the shot needs more sense of drama - more progression of light and shade, more three-dimensionality, than it has. I also think your sense of composition here is slightly askew - in that this is a very straightforward depiction of the flower. A good look through all the winning shots shows that there is a much more intense focus on shadow work, on a sense of landscape in the shots that have scored well than you have achieved here. Imagine, if you had focussed more clearly on the centre of the flower, and used the outer petals to frame that area, you would have the recognisable subject all the same, but with more immediate photographic impact. All of which presumes you are aiming simply to score well here, rather than submitting for any other reason. Outside of dpc-world, there is a feeling of odd light that I like very much in the centre of the flower: the very centre of the stamens seems to glow, and gives the impression of the flower emerging from the light of that area. However, even in this sense, I think you still need a greater sense of light and shade in the image. Along the stems of the petals there doesn''t seem to be much graduation between what should have been light areas and should have been dark ones - again, I suspect that this is as much a function of the auto-thing as of your capture of the image. Also, the inclusion of the greenery works against this - making more of the fact that it is simply a flower, rather than of the extraordinary elements at it''s centre - and puts the shot into a different category - one that is more of simple illustration. Whilst there is nothing wrong with that, it never seems to do that well here.  It could perhaps have been worked into something that would have scored better, but as it stands, i think if fully deserving of it''s ''average'' score. Ed', '2004-08-29 17:30:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(882865, 97950, 8891, '<td valign="top">Here''s the link to the final version:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=99889" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8891/thumb/99889.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8891/thumb/99889.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8891/thumb/99889.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Here''s the link to the final version: ', '2004-08-29 21:11:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(882953, 97966, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Wow fantastic focus here!  The flower just pops out ther eat you. Only thing I''m not to sure of in the photo is the dark corner.  My eye was pulled from the fantastic flower to the "black hole" of nothing so to speak.  You might want to try cropping it just slightly different.  In a whole though this is a fantastic entry.  Nice work.</td>', 'Critique Club Wow fantastic focus here!  The flower just pops out ther eat you. Only thing I''m not to sure of in the photo is the dark corner.  My eye was pulled from the fantastic flower to the "black hole" of nothing so to speak.  You might want to try cropping it just slightly different.  In a whole though this is a fantastic entry.  Nice work.', '2004-08-29 22:57:03.000000', NULL, 0),
